,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279128044,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkxMjgwNDQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/confirmed","name":"confirmed","color":"aaddaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2025-02-02T20:01:39Z","updated_at":"2025-05-19T21:12:21Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.4Beta1\n- Not reproducible in 4.3dev7\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.beta1 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1050 (NVIDIA; 31.0.15.5212) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-7300HQ CPU @ 2.50GHz (4 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nFloating game window is ignoring \"aspect\" settings. When set to  \"Mode -> canvas layer\" and \"Aspect ->expand\", no black bars should appear and the game should be stretched to cover the sides, but in Beta1 this stretching doesn't happen.\nAlso, with default settings \"Mode -> disabled\", black bars also appear, while in 4.4dev7 this was not the case, I wonder if this is intentional\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate new 2d scene and change settings in display -> Window to \"Mode -> canvas layer\" and \"Aspect ->expand\"\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18642303/mrp.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102334/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issue